#
# generate.rs drives mls-rs for every MLS structure (never the hub code
# under test): alice (mimi://a.example/u/alice) creates a group with
# BasicCredentials and adds bob (mimi://b.example/u/bob), once on
# ciphersuite 1 (group ID "suite1-fixture") and once on ciphersuite 3,
# MLS_128_DHKEMX25519_CHACHA20POLY1305_SHA256_Ed25519 (group ID
# "suite3-fixture"). Both GroupContexts carry the same hub rules:
# external_senders is exactly the RFC 8032 §7.1 TEST 1 Ed25519 public key
# with credential mimi://a.example, and an app_data_dictionary holds
# safe_aad requiring frank_aad (0x0020; bead mimid-1wgh.6.74),
# franking_agent (same key and credential), participant_list (alice, bob)
# and base_room_policy. alice's and bob's leaves list frank_aad in their
# own safe_aad lists. The component data comes from the shared test
# encoders in tests/common/mod.rs. The two groups differ only in
# ciphersuite, so the suite 1 control shows the suite 3 group breaks no
# other hub rule.
#
# It writes each structure exactly as mls-rs encodes it. mls-rs output is
# random, so regenerating writes new bytes; these files are the output of
# one run, unmodified.
#
